le areas but i think  there's probably three key takeaways  that i  i would want to stress right now one of  those areas is really that  this response to the pandemic has been  has been very positive and it's really  kind of re-emphasized the power of  collaborations in science  and both the collaborations within the  academic institute but also between  academic institutes and industry  partners as well as  um you know even seeing the the  collaborations between  uh potential competitors in the  industry groups it's been really  powerful to see this and  i really hope that that you know going  forward  that everybody sees the benefit of this  and  um you know we can really sustain this  down the road to move science along  quicker and  and bring new therapies and prevention  strategies to um  to the masses basically um i think the  other  area that this has really made me  recognize  um is the importance of of your team and  your family and dealing with these  [Music]  these stressors in these situations like  this we really need to take care of each  other  everybody really needs to um you know  help each other  get through these challenging times and  everybody deals with these  very differently so it's important that  we all check in with our team and  and that's not just your team at work  but your your family  uh team as well just to make sure  everybody's doing well and make sure  that  um you know we're all communicating and  getting the work done in a safe manner  and  and just you know keeping people uh you  know as happy as you can under the  conditions that that we're under  um and then lastly i think uh this is  really similar to what patricia said in  the  um you know thinking about the layout of  the lab we were  really fortunate in this um in this  situation that  our current space we were able to kind  of move things around and reconfigure  quite easily in order to operate with  minimal interactions between groups but  you know thinking about going 